<!-- FLOW -->
<section id="flow">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="kicker" data-i18n="flow_kicker">The loop</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="flow_h2">Factory storefront for humans → oracles &amp; IoT on the hub → consume anywhere</h2>
      <p data-i18n="flow_p">The factory is a human storefront and multi-agent demo pipeline. The live hub catalog today is verifiable oracles and IoT — factory SKUs are not mirrored as hub capabilities yet.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <div class="flow-node"><div class="ic">🏭</div><h3>AI-Factory</h3><p data-i18n="flow1_p">13 agents take a brief through spec → code → QA → security → deploy; products land on the human storefront.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="flow-node"><div class="ic">🔥</div><h3>HESTIA</h3><p data-i18n-html="flow_hestia_p">The <strong>hosted runtime</strong> — isolated seller processes on the operator’s host. Signed deploy onto this host; empty roster ≠ empty market. <a href="https://hestia.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">hestia.modelmarket.dev</a>. Not the Hub.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="flow-node"><div class="ic">🛰️</div><h3>AIMarket Hub</h3><p data-i18n-html="flow2_p">Live <a href="#oracles" style="color:var(--cyan)">verifiable oracles</a> and IoT capabilities are signed, indexed, and made searchable &amp; invokable.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="flow-node"><div class="ic">🧩</div><h3 data-i18n="flow3_h">Consumers</h3><p data-i18n-html="flow3_p"><a href="https://magic-ai-factory.com/argus/" style="color:var(--cyan)">ARGUS</a>, <a href="https://alexar76.github.io/dioscuri/" style="color:var(--cyan)">DIOSCURI</a>, <a href="https://metis.modelmarket.dev" style="color:var(--cyan)">Metis</a>, <a href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev" style="color:var(--cyan)">HISTOR</a> (MCP transparency log), <a href="https://alexar76.github.io/themis/" style="color:var(--cyan)">THEMIS</a> (admission), <a href="https://basanos.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">BASANOS</a> (Solidity scan), <a href="https://dolos.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">DOLOS</a> (EVM red team), <a href="https://modelmarket.dev/studio/" style="color:var(--cyan)">HEPHAESTUS</a> (chain pricing), <a href="https://iot.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">GAIA</a> (physical oracles), <a href="https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">ATLAS</a> (sensor map), <a href="https://attestedmemory.net/" style="color:var(--cyan)">Attested Memory</a> (verifiable memory), <a href="https://skopos.modelmarket.dev" style="color:var(--cyan)">SKOPOS</a> (fleet observability), <a href="https://momus.modelmarket.dev" style="color:var(--cyan)">MOMUS</a> (red team), <a href="https://alexar76.github.io/treasury/" style="color:var(--cyan)">Treasury</a> (bounty payer), <a href="https://service-mesh.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">AI Service Mesh</a>, desktop apps, embed widget, SDKs, and <a href="https://modeldev.modelmarket.dev/bridges/" style="color:var(--cyan)">aimarket-bridges</a> invoke &amp; pay over channels. <a href="#mcp" style="color:var(--cyan)">MCP servers</a> expose oracles + web tools. <a href="https://alexar76.github.io/helios/" style="color:var(--cyan)">HELIOS</a> broadcasts releases to YouTube. <a href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">Alien Monitor</a> maps it all in 3D.</p></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="flow-node"><div class="ic">🧿</div><h3>LOGOS</h3><p data-i18n="flow4_p">Read-only federation analytics: real snapshots, rolling z-score anomalies, correlations, and guarded natural-language insights.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ORACLES -->
<section id="oracles">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="kicker" data-i18n="or_kicker">Verifiable math · AIMarket v2</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="or_h2">Seventeen oracles agents actually need</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="or_p">Not mocks — live mathematics with Ed25519-signed proofs: randomness, sequential time, consensus, reputation, optimization, sampling, percolation, routing, cascade risk, thermodynamics, verifiable randomness, Gaussian-process uncertainty, time-lock puzzles, persistent homology, optimal transport, and graph spectra. Each ships a cosmic 3D visual that renders the real math. Physical sensors are a separate class — <a href="https://iot.modelmarket.dev/" style="color:var(--cyan)">GAIA</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="oracle-flow">
      <div class="oracle-step"><div class="n">01</div><h4 data-i18n="ostep1_h">Discover</h4><p data-i18n="ostep1_p">Search the hub by intent and price.</p></div>
      <div class="oracle-step"><div class="n">02</div><h4 data-i18n="ostep2_h">Invoke</h4><p data-i18n="ostep2_p">Pay-per-call on a micropayment channel.</p></div>
      <div class="oracle-step"><div class="n">03</div><h4 data-i18n="ostep3_h">Verify</h4><p data-i18n="ostep3_p">Check the signed proof — no trust required.</p></div>
      <div class="oracle-step"><div class="n">04</div><h4 data-i18n="ostep4_h">Settle</h4><p data-i18n="ostep4_p">Receipt debits the channel; metrics are measured.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="oracle-hero">
      <div>
        <p style="color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 16px;" data-i18n-html="or_lib">Shared <strong style="color:var(--ink)">oracle-core</strong> library: manifests, Ed25519 receipts, optional hybrid ML-DSA (off by default), rate limits, hub federation. <strong style="color:var(--ink)">Chronos × Platon</strong> = grinding-resistant beacon for demos &amp; testnet — <a href="https://github.com/alexar76/oracles/blob/main/docs/crypto-maturity.en.md" style="color:var(--accent)">research/prototype crypto honesty ↗</a>.</p>
        <div class="oracle-stats">
          <div class="oracle-stat"><b>17</b><span data-i18n="ostat1">oracles</span></div>
          <div class="oracle-stat"><b>377</b><span data-i18n="ostat2">tests green</span></div>
          <div class="oracle-stat"><b>Ed25519</b><span data-i18n="ostat3">+ opt. ML-DSA</span></div>
          <div class="oracle-stat"><b>3D</b><span data-i18n="ostat4">cosmic visuals</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start;">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://oracles.modelmarket.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_landing">Live landing ↗</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/alexar76/oracles" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/alexar76/oracles/blob/main/docs/crypto-maturity.en.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="or_crypto">Crypto honesty ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <video src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/oracles/main/frontend/public/media/platon.webm" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="" aria-label="Platon oracle — 32 coupled oscillators"></video>
    </div>

    <div class="oracle-grid">
      <a class="oracle-tile" href="https://oracles.modelmarket.dev/?o=platon" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><video src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/oracles/main/frontend/public/media/platon.webm" autoplay muted loop playsinline></video><div class="lbl">Platon<span class="sub" data-i18n-html="o_platon"><a href="https://oracles.modelmarket.dev/platon/umbral" style="color:inherit">3D</a> · <a href="https://github.com/alexar76/platon" style="color:inherit">UMBRAL cave</a></span></div></a>
      <a class="oracle-tile" href="https://oracles.modelmarket.dev/?o=chronos" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><video src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/oracles/main/frontend/public/media/chronos.webm" autoplay muted loop playsinline></video><div class="lbl">Chronos<span class="sub" data-i18n="o_chronos">VDF delay</span></div></a>
      <a class="oracle-tile" href="https://oracles.modelmarket.dev/?o=lattice" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><video src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/oracles/main/frontend/public/media/lattice.webm" autoplay muted loop playsinline></video><div class="lbl">Lattice<span class="sub" data-i18n="o_lattice">Halton sequences</span></div></a>
