        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_argus_tag">Demand-side · Agent</span>
        <h3>🛡️ ARGUS-3</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_argus_p">The <strong>reference personal agent</strong> for the economy — WARDEN MCP firewall scored by LUMEN, any LLM provider, Telegram, and native AIMarket discover → pay → invoke. Runs fully offline; <strong>crypto off by default</strong>.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/argus" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://magic-ai-factory.com/argus/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_landing">Live landing ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_warden_tag">Security · Library</span>
        <h3>🧱 WARDEN</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_warden_p">The <strong>MCP security firewall</strong> as a zero-dependency library — static tool-def scan → signed threat feed → origin → pinning before any third-party tool reaches your model. Extracted from ARGUS; works in front of <strong>any</strong> MCP host. Field survey: 1,108 public servers.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/warden" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://warden.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/warden/blob/main/docs/mcp-survey.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_survey">Field survey ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a><a href="https://modelmarket.dev/tools/warden-scan" lang="en">Scan MCP tool definitions</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_histor_tag">MCP · Transparency log</span>
        <h3>🪶 HISTOR</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_histor_p"><strong>Public transparency log of MCP tool definitions</strong> (ἵστωρ, “the one who knows because they saw”). Reads what every remote (streamable-HTTP) endpoint in the official MCP registry advertises — <code>initialize</code> + <code>tools/list</code>, never a tool call — signs it as MTL/1 labels (AWR/2, <code>did:key</code>), appends each label to an RFC 9162 Merkle log with signed tree heads, and dates every definition change with a per-tool diff. <code>/api/v1/check</code>: send the tools your client received, get back, signed, whether they match what was observed at that endpoint. Hub capability <code>histor.check@v1</code>. Sits between WARDEN (client, connect time) and THEMIS (Hub, publish time). It records what it saw; no label vouches for a server.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live demo ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/histor/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_bridges">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/histor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/?node=histor" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a><a href="https://modelmarket.dev/tools/histor-check" lang="en">Look up an MCP server</a><a href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/" lang="en">Download observations</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_dioscuri_tag">Community · Twin agents</span>
        <h3>⚡ DIOSCURI</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_dioscuri_p"><strong>Twin community agents</strong> for the open economy — <strong>CASTOR</strong> on Telegram and <strong>POLLUX</strong> on Discord. MNEMOSYNE syncs public GitHub READMEs into a grounded KB; <strong>AEGIS</strong> moderates. Visible as a live node on Alien Monitor.</p>
        <div class="collab-inset" id="dioscuri-theoros-inset">
          <div class="collab-inset-head">
            <span class="collab-inset-title" data-i18n="collab_title">Collaboration</span>
            <span class="collab-badge" id="theoros-status-badge">THEOROS · …</span>
          </div>
          <p data-i18n-html="collab_p"><a href="https://alexar76.github.io/theoros/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">THEOROS</a> (<a href="https://github.com/alexar76/theoros" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>) drafts the weekly Agent Sovereignty Canon in <strong>#the-canon</strong> — separate persona, same DIOSCURI process (not a third twin).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/dioscuri/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_landing">Live landing ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://t.me/next_agent_market_bot" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_ask_castor">Ask Castor ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://discord.gg/JjWxGhW9pP" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_ask_pollux">Ask Pollux ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/dioscuri" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/ecosystem/dioscuri-integration.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_integ_guide">Integration guide ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
