      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_helios_tag">Broadcast · DevRel</span>
        <h3>☀️ HELIOS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_helios_p"><strong>Self-hosted broadcast pipeline</strong> — yaml template in, voiced video out, queued to YouTube <strong>private until you approve</strong>. POST-only, no engagement bots. Backfills PromoMaterials backlog, then release-shorts on ship.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/helios/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_landing">Live landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/helios" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/ecosystem/helios-integration.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_integ_guide">Integration guide ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://www.youtube.com/@My-AI-Factory" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_metis_tag">Reasoning · Verification</span>
        <h3>🧠 Metis</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_metis_p">A <strong>distributed cognitive layer over any LLM</strong> — Understanding Council, fail-closed confidence gate, layered Mixture-of-Agents and a grounded verifier. It deliberates and verifies before answering and returns a machine-readable confidence score; a <strong>capability gate</strong> keeps weak models out of key roles. The AI-Factory calls it as a confidence gate; live as a cognition node on Alien Monitor.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://metis.modelmarket.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live demo ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/metis/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">3D landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/metis" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-metis/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PyPI ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/metis-integration.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_integ">Integration ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_themis_tag">Admission · Supply chain</span>
        <h3>🛡 THEMIS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_themis_p"><strong>Publish-time admission gate</strong> for AIMarket — signed <code>approve</code> / <code>review</code> / <code>reject</code> before the Hub lists a third-party agent, MCP server, or plugin. Not Metis cognition; not WARDEN runtime. Hub modes <code>off</code> / <code>advisory</code> / <code>enforce</code> — pin an auditor key and verdicts are recorded; blocking still takes an explicit <code>enforce</code>.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/themis/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://alexar76.github.io/themis/console/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_console">Console ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/themis" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/create-aimarket-agent/blob/main/docs/tutorials/themis.en.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_docs">Tutorial ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/ecosystem/supply-chain-admission.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_integ">Admission ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_hestia_tag">Hosted runtime · Hosting control plane</span>
        <h3>🔥 HESTIA</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_hestia_p"><strong>Isolated hosted runtime</strong> for AIMarket capability providers on the operator’s machines. Not the Hub catalogue, not Factory, not a job board. Agents appear only after an explicit signed deploy onto this host; an empty roster is not an empty market. Optional THEMIS admit; announce is explicit; Hub stays the market.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://hestia.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live demo ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/hestia/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/hestia" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_attested_tag">Memory · Agents</span>
        <h3>🧠 Attested Memory</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_attested_p"><strong>Verifiable memory for AI agents</strong> — Memory Market (write, search, share), Truth Layer (evidence and contradictions) and Provenance Ledger (lineage, signed receipts) around one Memory Unit contract, with MCP. Self-hosted, Docker.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://attestedmemory.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live demo ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/attested-memory/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/attested-memory" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_basanos_tag">Contracts · Assurance</span>
        <h3>🪨 BASANOS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_basanos_p"><strong>Solidity touchstone</strong> for ecosystem contracts — scans at a pinned commit and emits Ed25519-signed <code>PASS</code> / <code>REVIEW</code> / <code>FAIL</code> packs with evidence and an operator playbook. Technical assurance, not insurance or catalogue admission.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://basanos.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live console ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/basanos/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/basanos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_dolos_tag">EVM · Dynamic red team</span>
        <h3>⚔️ DOLOS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_dolos_p"><strong>Dynamic EVM red team</strong> for the UNI bubble — forks Anvil, throws real exploit transactions to prove which flaws are live vs static noise, emits Ed25519-signed findings. Auto fix-loop only on sandbox <code>chainId 31337</code>; mainnet findings stay advisory. Sibling to BASANOS (static) and MOMUS (HTTP/federation).</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://dolos.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/dolos/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pages ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/dolos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <!-- LOGOS -->
      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_logos_tag">Analytics · Federation · AI</span>
        <h3>🧿 LOGOS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_logos_p">A <strong>read-only federation analytics engine</strong> — real Hub snapshots and measured settlement volume, rolling z-score anomaly detection, cross-source correlations, natural-language insights via Metis, and a guarded AI assistant. Unreachable sources stay explicitly unavailable; they never become fake zeroes.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://logos.modelmarket.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_dash">Live dashboard ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/logos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/logos/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/logos#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_docs">Docs ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_gaia_tag">Physical oracles · IoT</span>
        <h3>🌍 GAIA</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_gaia_p"><strong>Physical-world oracle gateway</strong> — third class beside math oracles (×17) and Metis. Live public relays on the Hub today: Open-Meteo weather/AQ, UK grid carbon, USGS quakes, NOAA tides (+ sim fleet). Ed25519-attested, plausibility-verified. Same discover → channel → invoke → settle loop.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://iot.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live demo ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/gaia/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">3D landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/gaia" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/iot-physical-oracles.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_docs">Docs ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>


      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_atlas_tag">Sensor map · GAIA</span>
        <h3>🗺 ATLAS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_atlas_p"><strong>Planetary physical-sensor map</strong> over GAIA relays — honest <strong>LIVE</strong> vs <strong>SIM</strong> pins (weather, air, tide, grid, quake, energy), Alien Monitor embed, and ATLAS Analyst grounded on the server snapshot <em>plus</em> a full AICOM / AIMarket ecosystem brief (Hub, ARGUS, Metis, oracles…).</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live map ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/atlas/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/atlas" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/atlas/blob/main/docs/GUIDE.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_docs">Docs ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_esim_tag">Real goods · x402</span>
        <h3>📶 eSIM operator kit</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_esim_p"><strong>Travel eSIMs sold to people and AI agents.</strong> A storefront for people and a seller node agents pay over x402 in USDC, straight to the operator's wallet; refunds of unused eSIMs and signed delivery receipts the Hub counts as confirmed deliveries. Operators join in one command, <code>./onboard.sh</code>, as a federation node or their own hub.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://esim.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_esim_demo">Demo seller ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://esim.modelmarket.dev/kit" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_esim_guides">Guides ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/esim-operator-kit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/?node=modelmarket-dev-demo-esim-seller" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>


      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_hunt_tag">Game · Federation lab</span>
        <h3>🔍 Signal Hunt</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_hunt_p"><strong>Federation-native investigation game</strong> and educational lab over real Hub telemetry — observe a measured symptom, open committed evidence, commit a diagnosis, get a Brier-score verdict. No seeded anomaly feed.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://hunt.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live hunt ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/signal-hunt/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/signal-hunt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/signal-hunt/blob/main/docs/GUIDE.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_docs">Docs ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_usecases_tag">GTM · Onboarding</span>
        <h3>🧭 Use-cases portal</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_usecases_p"><strong>Public wow + onboarding + direction boards</strong> — verifiable provenance to agent economy, callable products, honest LIVE vs SIM maturity chips, five languages. Pages landing CTAs into the live host.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://use.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live portal ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/use-cases-portal/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/use-cases-portal" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_skopos_tag">Observability</span>
        <h3>🛰️ SKOPOS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_skopos_p"><strong>Fleet observability satellite</strong> — nginx &amp; Apache analytics over SSH, Security Center with 3D threat map, scan history, and an AI analyst. Self-hosted data; <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> recommended for production. Live node on Alien Monitor with public <code>/healthz</code> metrics.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://skopos.modelmarket.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_dash">Live dashboard ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/skopos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/ecosystem/skopos-integration.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_integ">Integration ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>


      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_momus_tag">Red team · Signed findings</span>
        <h3>👁 MOMUS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_momus_p"><strong>Autonomous red team</strong> — safe read-only conformance probes against the ecosystem's own components; Ed25519-signed findings; self-learning (UCB + public threat intel). Honest outcomes: FINDING / NO_FINDING / INCONCLUSIVE. <strong>Finds and signs but cannot pay itself.</strong></p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://momus.modelmarket.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live demo ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/momus/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/momus" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_inmon">In Monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_treasury_tag">Bounty payer · Separation of duties</span>
        <h3>🏦 Treasury</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_treasury_p"><strong>Separate bounty payer</strong> for MOMUS findings — its own key and container. Verifies signatures, recomputes dedup identity, releases finder/fixer/conductor split (50/35/15) only after independent verification. MOMUS finds; Treasury pays.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://momus.modelmarket.dev/treasury" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_demo">Live ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/treasury/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_3dland">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/treasury" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_monitor_tag">3D visualization</span>
        <h3>👽 Alien Monitor</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_monitor_p">Real-time <strong>3D visualization</strong> of the whole ecosystem — Hub, Factory, <strong>ARGUS</strong>, contracts, agents, and on-chain metrics in one interactive cosmic graph. No login required.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/alien-monitor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://monitor.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_monitor">Live monitor ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_pulse_tag">Markets · ACEX</span>
        <h3>📈 Pulse Terminal</h3>
        <p data-i18n="p_pulse_p">A capital-markets dashboard for the agent economy — live CapShare NAV, revenue indices, and WebSocket pricing streamed from the factory.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/pulse-terminal" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://pulse.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_term">Live terminal ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/acex" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ACEX ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_widget_tag">Embed</span>
        <h3>🔌 AIMarket Widget</h3>
        <p data-i18n="p_widget_p">A drop-in widget that puts federated AI search + invoke on any website with one snippet. The 1-click on-ramp to the whole marketplace.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-widget" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>


      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_bridges_tag">Bridges</span>
        <h3>🌉 aimarket-bridges</h3>
        <p data-i18n="p_bridges_p">LangGraph, CrewAI, AutoGen and Agent Framework adapters — turn live Hub capabilities into native framework tools with signed receipts and budget caps.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-bridges" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a><a class="demo" href="https://modeldev.modelmarket.dev/bridges/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_bridges">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://modeldev.modelmarket.dev/guides/aimarket-bridges/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_guide">Guide ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_sdks_tag">SDKs</span>
        <h3>🧰 Client SDKs</h3>
        <p data-i18n="p_sdks_p">Python, Dart, TypeScript, and Rust client libraries for discovering and invoking capabilities — the same surface the desktop apps and widget are built on.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_desktop_tag">Apps</span>
        <h3>🖥️ Desktop SKUs</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_desktop_p">Eight Flutter desktop apps sharing one core, plus a standalone Rust <em>Local Security Audit</em> SKU that scans a repo for secrets &amp; CVEs fully offline.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-desktop" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_plugins_tag">Plugins</span>
        <h3>🧱 Hub Plugins</h3>
        <p data-i18n="p_plugins_p">Pip-installable plugins that hook the hub's invoke lifecycle — safety, compliance, routing, and custom capability adapters.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-plugins" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_contracts_tag">Settlement</span>
        <h3>⛓️ Payment Contracts</h3>
        <p data-i18n="p_contracts_p">EVM + Solana non-custodial USDT payment channels. Users deposit directly; a 24h auto-refund path depends on no privileged account. No upgradable proxies.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/tree/main/contracts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_horkos_tag">Settlement · Escrow policy signer</span>
        <h3>🔏 HORKOS</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_horkos_p"><strong>Escrow policy signer</strong> — holds the only key authorized in <code>AIMarketEscrow.authorizedHubs</code>, so the Hub does not: one allowed selector, one escrow, one chain, and the buyer’s own EIP-712 signature as the authority for every amount.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://alexar76.github.io/escrow-signer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_bridges">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/escrow-signer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_linkedin_tag">Integrated app · example</span>
        <h3>💼 LinkedIn Profile Coach</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_linkedin_p">An <strong>ecosystem-integrated app</strong> in the same class as the desktop SKUs (Flutter + AIMarket SDK), with its own focus: <strong>LinkedIn profile improvement</strong> — import, scoring, compare, and AI drafts.</p>
        <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/linked-in-profile-coach" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="tag" data-i18n="p_cite_tag">Evidence desks · On AIMarket rails</span>
        <h3>📑 Cite desks</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="p_cite_p"><strong>Independent evidence desks</strong> on AIMarket rails — one parent repo: a shared kernel plus fire, flood, PV, Nordic AIS and site desks, each a nested project with its own README. Family landing at desk.modelmarket.dev; not an AIMarket brand surface.</p>
        <div class="links"><a class="demo" href="https://desk.modelmarket.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="L_bridges">Landing ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/cite-desks" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>

    </div>
